<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! realm.walk.reads ~ walk ~ where this vessel walks

Bare `lares walk` reads, per hearth this vessel walks at: the Nexus, the relay, whether its invite still waits for a dial to redeem it, the grant it holds (its epoch, lineage and rolls survived), and how many invites its wallet holds. A vessel walks at one hearth, as one face. The act runs inside the standing vessel, else here under this command's own key session.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ none

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ custody

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`custody` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ one sealed act frame on the custody door under the vessel key; the walk record never rests in the clear`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ refused · error

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`refused` params=`~ the custody door refused the act; the message names why`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`error` params=`~ the act failed outside the door's refusals`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ walks

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`walks` params=`exit/0 fields/[[walks via]] ~ each walk, and via naming daemon or direct`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ cli

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/cli`>>

!!! lares walk

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`cli` params=`handler/host spells/[[lares walk]] ~ the terminal`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

